  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "read_committed: The Consumer Side of EOS",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Prove It, Don't Assume",
          "items": [
            "Kill brokers mid-batch",
            "Kill consumers mid-transaction",
            "Count output keys afterwards",
            "One stray default downgrades you to at-least-once"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Latency Costs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`acks=0`: one network hop, no wait",
            "`acks=all`: leader + slowest in-sync replica",
            "Idempotence: typically low single-digit percent",
            "One sequence number per batch, plus broker state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Transaction Cost Is Per Batch"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Charged per transaction, not per record",
            "Amortize by batching more records into one",
            "Two extra coordinator round trips",
            "Plus one control marker per touched partition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Batch style",
            "Throughput hit"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tiny transactions",
              "~20%"
            ],
            [
              "large batches",
              "~3%"
            ],
            [
              "Confluent range",
              "3-20%"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Latency Floor",
          "text": "For a `read_committed` consumer the floor is the transaction duration — nothing is visible before commit. Streams defaults near a 100ms commit interval for exactly this balance."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Levers That Matter More"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`linger.ms` and `batch.size` beat any EOS knob",
            "Batching amortizes everything downstream",
            "`compression.type=lz4` or `zstd` cuts network and disk",
            "Compression is per batch: bigger batches compress better"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Broker-Side Bill"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Memory grows with live PIDs and open transactions",
            "Many short-lived producers is an anti-pattern",
            "`__transaction_state` and `__consumer_offsets` are real topics",
            "Real writes, real replication, real disk",
            "Rebalances cost more: open transactions abort and replay"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pick By Number"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Semantic",
            "Throughput",
            "Safety"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "highest",
              "lowest"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "~95%",
              "no loss"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "80-95%",
              "full"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Decision Guide",
          "items": [
            "Start with at-least-once plus an idempotent sink",
            "Reach for transactions only if the sink can't dedupe",
            "100ms commit interval is a sane starting size"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why did EOS halve my throughput?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Transactions too small: coordinator cost dominates",
            "Raise `linger.ms`, batch more per transaction",
            "Check rebalance rate — each abort replays work"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "read_committed: The Consumer Side of EOS (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Durability Lies",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`acks=all` with `min.insync.replicas=1` is not durable",
            "A single-replica window loses committed data",
            "`unclean.leader.election.enable=true` in an HA config",
            "It trades committed data for uptime"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs: Throughput, Latency, Cost",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Slips That Downgrade You"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`enable.auto.commit=true` inside a transactional app",
            "Offsets then commit outside the transaction",
            "Downstream left at `read_uncommitted`",
            "Then aborted records show up and confuse everyone"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "`transactional.id` habit",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "reused across instances",
              "fencing loop"
            ],
            [
              "random at startup",
              "zombie keeps writing"
            ],
            [
              "stable and unique",
              "correct fencing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Silent At-Most-Once"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ignoring the `send()` callback exception",
            "Calling `future.get()` nowhere",
            "Committing offsets before processing",
            "That is choosing loss, not avoiding duplicates"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fatal, Do Not Retry"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ProducerFencedException`",
            "`OutOfOrderSequenceException`",
            "Authorization errors",
            "Close the producer and exit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Loop Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Processing slower than `max.poll.interval.ms`",
            "Rebalance loop, endless reprocessing",
            "Lower `max.poll.records`",
            "Or use a worker thread plus `consumer.pause()`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Things EOS Never Covers",
          "items": [
            "External email or HTTP calls fire twice on replay",
            "A long transaction stalls LSO for every reader",
            "`max.in.flight`>1 without idempotence reorders",
            "Retention or compaction deleting unread records"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Retention loss looks exactly like delivery loss to a lagging consumer. Check retention before blaming `acks`."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Read The Duplicates",
          "text": "Matching offsets twice means consumer-side redelivery. Different offsets with the same payload means a producer-side resend."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Config Sets",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Target",
            "Key settings",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "`acks=0`, auto-commit",
              "metrics, traces"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "`acks=all`, manual commit",
              "most systems"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "+ `transactional.id`",
              "ledgers, billing"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs: Throughput, Latency, Cost (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "At-most-once: async handoff, sampled telemetry",
            "At-least-once: idempotence on, `min.insync.replicas=2`",
            "At-least-once is the correct default for most systems",
            "Exactly-once adds `sendOffsetsToTransaction` and `read_committed`"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Failure Modes and Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Guarantee Ladder"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "no acks",
              "acks=all",
              "idempotence",
              "transactions",
              "read_committed"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Each Knob Kills One Failure"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "Kills"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Idempotent producer",
              "retry duplicates"
            ],
            [
              "Transactions",
              "partial writes"
            ],
            [
              "`read_committed`",
              "aborted reads"
            ],
            [
              "`acks=all`",
              "leader-death loss"
            ],
            [
              "`min.insync.replicas=2`",
              "single-replica loss"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Defaults Worth Memorising",
          "items": [
            "`enable.idempotence=true` since 3.0",
            "`acks=all` since 3.0",
            "`isolation.level=read_uncommitted` always"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cheapest Big Win"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Turn on idempotence, set `min.insync.replicas=2`",
            "Near-zero cost, kills the common dup and loss paths",
            "Prefer an upsert-keyed sink over transactions",
            "Especially when you control the sink schema"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "var off = new OffsetAndMetadata(",
            "    rec.offset() + 1);  // always +1",
            "// under read_committed offsets are",
            "// not contiguous: markers take slots"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Verify With Chaos",
          "items": [
            "Kill the leader mid-produce",
            "Kill the consumer mid-transaction",
            "Assert output counts by key"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Monitor consumer lag and LSO lag",
            "Monitor transaction abort rate",
            "Monitor producer `record-error-rate`",
            "Streams `exactly_once_v2`: shortest correct path"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Slips, One Table"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Slip",
            "Silent result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "auto-commit left on",
              "offsets escape txn"
            ],
            [
              "`read_uncommitted`",
              "aborted rows appear"
            ],
            [
              "`min.insync.replicas=1`",
              "single-replica loss"
            ],
            [
              "random `transactional.id`",
              "zombie writes on"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Chaos Run"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Produce 10k keyed records under EOS",
            "Kill the leader broker mid-batch",
            "Kill one consumer mid-transaction",
            "Group output by key, assert count = 1",
            "Any key at 2 means a broken link"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Read The Symptom",
          "text": "Lag climbing with zero progress means a stuck transaction pinning the LSO. Duplicates at matching offsets mean consumer redelivery, not producer resend."
        }
      ]
    },
